{"id": "EUVD-2026-101140", "enisaUuid": "85039a13-b0fe-3cad-8845-9b220a5c481f", "description": "Janus WebRTC Server through 1.4.3 contains a path traversal vulnerability in the Record&Play plugin that allows unauthenticated attackers to write files outside recordings_path via the record request filename. Attackers can supply filenames with path separators to create or truncate files ending in -audio.mjr, -video.mjr or -data.mjr anywhere the Janus process can write outside protected folders.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T15:01:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T17:40:56", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@1ExmmukzRMWN7B4gQ4W-4Q/HkEaF-piGl", "https://github.com/meetecho/janus-gateway/blob/1f0b75cac1c9ad819ee4c2a905a2c65b00b82cde/src/plugins/janus_recordplay.c#L1965", "https://github.com/meetecho/janus-gateway/blob/1f0b75cac1c9ad819ee4c2a905a2c65b00b82cde/src/record.c#L218", "https://github.com/meetecho/janus-gateway", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/janus-webrtc-server-through-1.4.3-path-traversal-via-record-play-filename"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110717", "GHSA-rwr7-3rqr-7qwv"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.46, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "4967641f-dda4-354b-ab15-4b322f50fb48", "product": {"name": "janus-gateway", "vendor": {"name": "meetecho"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.4.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "907889a7-d2d9-3b9a-be4d-60b1ad2705cc", "vendor": {"name": "meetecho"}}], "isExploited": false}